From d018aeebf590d3136c7d2014b7c43ba72ee6e1ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knfsd-fuzz <knfsd-fuzz@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sys/linux, executor: add a lane client network partition

A lane client can stop talking to its server without the harness acting
on the server: syz_nfs_lane_link$partition_client0 gives the client's
only link in its own lane network namespace a blackhole root qdisc for
15 s, longer than the single fixture's 10 s NFSv4 lease, and returns
with the qdisc still in place.  syz_nfs_lane_link$heal_client0 deletes
it.  Each call fails with EALREADY unless it changes the link.

The blackhole qdisc drops every packet the client sends and reports
success, so the client sees a silent network rather than a local error,
and the link keeps its addresses and routes.  A link taken down instead
makes the client's lease renewal fail with ENETUNREACH and drops the
lane's static route to the second server address.

partition carries a 16 s call timeout so the executor waits for it, and
heal a 30 s program timeout so the client's recovery requests that
follow it, which wait on TCP retransmission backoff, finish inside the
program.  The fork server deletes every lane client's qdisc after each
program, so no partition outlives the program that made it.
